1
00:01:07,080 --> 00:01:09,280
(Stone Coffin - 2)

2
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:11,200
Ching Sir, we got something.

3
00:01:11,280 --> 00:01:11,880
What?

4
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:15,320
Just got word, a Hong Kong girl in her 20s

5
00:01:15,400 --> 00:01:16,480
showed up at the Police station

6
00:01:16,560 --> 00:01:18,480
and claimed she was Suet from
the stone coffin case.

7
00:01:18,560 --> 00:01:19,920
Of her own free will?

8
00:01:20,120 --> 00:01:21,760
Yes. She came to turn herself in
Don't move!

9
00:01:27,480 --> 00:01:28,080
(Six months later)

10
00:01:28,160 --> 00:01:28,880
Court!

11
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:36,000
Tai Yat-kin,

12
00:01:36,120 --> 00:01:38,800
how did you meet the victim Lau Yue-bun?

13
00:01:38,920 --> 00:01:42,400
Through a friend of a friend.

14
00:01:42,520 --> 00:01:44,320
The banker wanted to make quick money.

15
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:46,760
I happened to know the owner of a casino

16
00:01:46,880 --> 00:01:47,960
who wanted to launder money.

17
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:49,600
So I brought them together.

18
00:01:49,800 --> 00:01:51,280
We started out OK.

19
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:52,880
After we split up the money a few times,

20
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:54,400
he got greedy.

21
00:01:54,560 --> 00:01:56,480
We often got into arguments.

22
00:01:56,960 --> 00:02:00,440
That loser made money all thanks to me.

23
00:02:01,240 --> 00:02:04,440
He got so cocky, just knife him.

24
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:09,840
Don't do that. A waste of effort and energy.

25
00:02:10,760 --> 00:02:14,080
Pour petrol on his hands.

26
00:02:14,200 --> 00:02:17,200
Light him up and teach him a lesson.

27
00:02:17,320 --> 00:02:19,920
Forget the lesson. Just kill him!

28
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:22,440
It was your suggestion to kill him?

29
00:02:22,560 --> 00:02:25,360
No, I was just saying it.

30
00:02:25,520 --> 00:02:27,920
When you're drunk, you're capable of
saying anything.

31
00:02:28,040 --> 00:02:31,280
I was worried Dummy and Shek would
take me seriously,

32
00:02:31,440 --> 00:02:33,160
so when I sobered up the next day,

33
00:02:33,280 --> 00:02:35,120
I made sure I told them I was just kidding.

34
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:37,840
No, I didn't hear Brother Kin say
he was just kidding.

35
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:40,840
I didn't hear him say he was kidding.

36
00:02:40,920 --> 00:02:44,280
I only heard him say "just kill him".

37
00:02:44,360 --> 00:02:47,920
The next day, the dude came up on his own.

38
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:49,200
By "the next day",

39
00:02:49,360 --> 00:02:50,640
you mean the day he was killed?

40
00:02:50,800 --> 00:02:54,880
Yes, I went out with Dummy to get some food.

41
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:58,320
When we went back upstairs, we saw the dude.

42
00:02:58,480 --> 00:02:59,920
Next time, remember to lock the door.

43
00:03:00,040 --> 00:03:00,880
Right...

44
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:05,840
Hey! What are you looking for?

45
00:03:05,960 --> 00:03:07,400
I came to get what is mine.

46
00:03:07,640 --> 00:03:08,720
Your Brother Kin owes me $500K.

47
00:03:08,840 --> 00:03:09,920
That's my money.

48
00:03:10,080 --> 00:03:11,440
Who cares how much you're making,

49
00:03:11,520 --> 00:03:12,720
as long as you're making money.

50
00:03:12,840 --> 00:03:14,160
That's easy for you to say.

51
00:03:14,240 --> 00:03:16,640
I'm the one living in fear.

52
00:03:16,720 --> 00:03:18,720
If anyone found out, I'm going to jail.

53
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:19,760
Man the hell up!

54
00:03:19,880 --> 00:03:21,040
What's a few years in the cell?

55
00:03:21,160 --> 00:03:23,400
That's easy for you to say, you're not
going to jail.

56
00:03:23,520 --> 00:03:25,000
I don't care. I want my money.

57
00:03:25,680 --> 00:03:26,400
What are you doing?

58
00:03:27,320 --> 00:03:28,840
Who made you the Boss? You have no say.

59
00:03:28,920 --> 00:03:30,880
Dummy, get Brother Kin down here.

60
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:33,040
You, stay where you are!

61
00:03:33,440 --> 00:03:33,920
Brother Kin...

62
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:35,280
The night before, Brother Kin got blasted.

63
00:03:35,400 --> 00:03:35,920
Wake up, Brother Kin!

64
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:37,440
Ben is here...
I went upstairs to try to wake him...

65
00:03:37,560 --> 00:03:38,880
He came for the money...
But I couldn't wake him...

66
00:03:38,960 --> 00:03:40,160
There was nothing I could do,

67
00:03:40,240 --> 00:03:41,760
so I went back downstairs.

68
00:03:41,880 --> 00:03:43,560
Shek...
Let's figure out what to do.

69
00:03:43,680 --> 00:03:44,320
Shek...

70
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:46,160
I asked Shek if we were going to kill him.

71
00:03:46,280 --> 00:03:47,920
But we didn't buy any tools.

72
00:03:48,080 --> 00:03:50,800
Soon the dude found the safe.

73
00:03:51,520 --> 00:03:54,000
Stop it! What do you want?

74
00:03:54,120 --> 00:03:55,160
Stand back!

75
00:03:55,240 --> 00:03:57,280
Stay back...open the safe!

76
00:03:57,400 --> 00:03:58,320
I want my money!

77
00:03:58,400 --> 00:03:59,440
I'll get the combination from Brother Kin.

78
00:03:59,520 --> 00:04:00,720
Move...
Bloody hell!

79
00:04:01,440 --> 00:04:02,400
Come out...

80
00:04:10,640 --> 00:04:12,480
Dummy, get a rope and tie him up.

81
00:04:13,960 --> 00:04:15,520
Tie him up!

82
00:04:15,640 --> 00:04:16,560
We have rope?

83
00:04:16,640 --> 00:04:17,760
Go find it!

84
00:04:18,160 --> 00:04:21,200
Before we know it, something else happened.

85
00:04:23,520 --> 00:04:24,320
Who is it?

86
00:04:24,400 --> 00:04:25,080
(Unknown caller)

87
00:04:25,200 --> 00:04:27,280
Are you the owner of LJ3314?

88
00:04:27,360 --> 00:04:28,960
Your car is in my way.

89
00:04:29,080 --> 00:04:30,320
Get over here and move it!

90
00:04:30,400 --> 00:04:31,840
Or else I'm calling the Police!

91
00:04:31,920 --> 00:04:32,840
Go move the car! Go...

92
00:04:32,960 --> 00:04:34,520
OK, I'll go...

93
00:04:42,400 --> 00:04:43,040
Hello?

94
00:04:44,080 --> 00:04:45,600
I forgot the key!

95
00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:47,680
What's wrong with you?

96
00:04:47,840 --> 00:04:49,280
I'm taking it down now.

97
00:04:55,720 --> 00:04:57,200
When is your friend coming?

98
00:04:57,320 --> 00:04:58,160
Don't you know how to park a car?

99
00:04:58,280 --> 00:04:59,360
He's coming...

100
00:04:59,440 --> 00:05:00,560
What's going on?
Or else...

101
00:05:00,640 --> 00:05:02,400
Look at the way he parked his car!

102
00:05:02,520 --> 00:05:03,040
You wish to call the Police?

103
00:05:03,120 --> 00:05:03,920
Officer!

104
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:05,960
I'm leaving...Sorry...
Coming...

105
00:05:06,080 --> 00:05:08,160
Very sorry...
Move it...

106
00:05:08,240 --> 00:05:09,200
Right...

107
00:05:09,280 --> 00:05:10,480
We moved the car

108
00:05:10,560 --> 00:05:11,840
and parked it as far away as possible.

109
00:05:11,920 --> 00:05:13,440
When we got back to the industrial building,

110
00:05:13,520 --> 00:05:15,600
Ben lost a lot a blood.

111
00:05:15,960 --> 00:05:17,440
Is he dead?

112
00:05:17,720 --> 00:05:19,200
People don't die so easily...

113
00:05:19,400 --> 00:05:22,000
Why did you ram his head against the wall?

114
00:05:22,080 --> 00:05:23,960
His head hit a nail!

115
00:05:24,920 --> 00:05:27,520
It was Shek who grabbed Ben

116
00:05:27,600 --> 00:05:28,800
and hit his head on the wall.

117
00:05:28,920 --> 00:05:30,640
His head hit a nail.

118
00:05:31,400 --> 00:05:33,960
Get Brother Kin...

119
00:05:34,480 --> 00:05:38,800
The night before, I was up drinking
all night with friends.

120
00:05:39,080 --> 00:05:41,080
I totally blacked out.

121
00:05:41,200 --> 00:05:43,760
When I woke up, I saw Dummy and Shek...

122
00:05:43,840 --> 00:05:46,400
They came upstairs and told me
they killed someone.

123
00:05:46,600 --> 00:05:48,240
I went downstairs to take a look

124
00:05:48,360 --> 00:05:51,840
and saw Ben lying by the wall.

125
00:05:52,520 --> 00:05:54,640
There was massive bleeding behind his head

126
00:05:54,720 --> 00:05:55,400
and he was dead.

127
00:05:55,520 --> 00:05:58,880
They then decided to put the body
in a stone coffin

128
00:05:58,960 --> 00:06:00,640
and throw it in the sea.

129
00:06:00,720 --> 00:06:02,160
So I gave them a hand.

130
00:06:08,080 --> 00:06:09,040
We didn't call for a ride.

131
00:06:09,160 --> 00:06:09,760
What?

132
00:06:10,080 --> 00:06:11,520
Wait downstairs.

133
00:06:16,920 --> 00:06:18,640
A little bit off...
Come on...

134
00:06:19,920 --> 00:06:20,960
Close the door...

135
00:06:21,640 --> 00:06:24,480
Stop! Gotcha!

136
00:06:27,800 --> 00:06:29,920
Your crate looks heavy.

137
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:32,560
It's huge. What's inside?

138
00:06:34,600 --> 00:06:35,280
What's going on?

139
00:06:35,400 --> 00:06:37,360
Nothing...just a misunderstanding.

140
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:40,480
You two...this is not the goods
for the client.

141
00:06:40,640 --> 00:06:41,640
Go back in and get the right one.

142
00:06:41,800 --> 00:06:42,560
Right...

143
00:06:42,640 --> 00:06:44,240
Get out of the way...
You go ahead, sorry!

144
00:06:44,360 --> 00:06:47,600
Sorry...excuse us...
Hurry up! Don't hold her up...

145
00:06:48,920 --> 00:06:51,840
But we simply can't move the stone coffin.

146
00:06:52,040 --> 00:06:54,880
We knew we can't keep it under wraps
for much longer.

147
00:06:55,040 --> 00:06:56,520
So we planned to skip town.

148
00:06:56,640 --> 00:06:58,520
If you were not involved in the killing,

149
00:06:58,640 --> 00:07:00,320
why did you help them with hiding the body

150
00:07:00,400 --> 00:07:01,280
and go on the run together?

151
00:07:01,480 --> 00:07:03,600
That's brotherhood.

152
00:07:03,760 --> 00:07:06,480
They're in trouble, I can't watch them fry.

153
00:07:06,560 --> 00:07:09,600
Besides, a friend loaned me the unit,

154
00:07:09,680 --> 00:07:12,320
if word go out about what happened,

155
00:07:12,920 --> 00:07:14,720
I can't deny my involvement anyway.

156
00:07:14,800 --> 00:07:16,240
You're not worried about getting arrested?

157
00:07:16,360 --> 00:07:19,520
Yes, that's why we went into hiding.

158
00:07:19,600 --> 00:07:21,200
We thought we could get away.

159
00:07:21,840 --> 00:07:25,520
But the cops caught onto the
fake bank accounts,

160
00:07:25,920 --> 00:07:27,520
and eventually found Ben's body.

161
00:07:27,640 --> 00:07:29,760
Are you working for a criminal syndicate?

162
00:07:29,920 --> 00:07:30,880
Who's the real boss?

163
00:07:30,960 --> 00:07:33,640
I was a jailbird.

164
00:07:33,760 --> 00:07:37,280
A petty thief like me won't know
any big shots.

165
00:07:37,400 --> 00:07:40,480
I'm incapable of committing felonies.

166
00:07:40,640 --> 00:07:42,640
I can't even kill a cockroach.

167
00:07:44,040 --> 00:07:46,880
Your Honor, I wish to put Ho Pui-suet,

168
00:07:46,960 --> 00:07:48,560
the immunized witness on the stand.

169
00:07:51,600 --> 00:07:55,440
Ho Pui-suet, how did you meet
the victim Lau Yue-bun?

170
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:57,280
Strictly speaking, I don't know him.

171
00:07:57,400 --> 00:08:01,520
I heard from Brother Kin, Dummy and Shek

172
00:08:01,640 --> 00:08:04,080
they had an argument with the banker dude.

173
00:08:04,160 --> 00:08:06,480
The banker dude should be Lau Yue-bun.

174
00:08:06,560 --> 00:08:08,480
What were you doing at the time
of the incident?

175
00:08:08,600 --> 00:08:09,920
I was sleeping upstairs.

176
00:08:10,040 --> 00:08:11,200
Have you heard anything?

177
00:08:11,800 --> 00:08:12,880
No.

178
00:08:13,080 --> 00:08:15,840
The victim was downstairs arguing
and fighting

179
00:08:15,960 --> 00:08:17,640
with Cheung Sai-chor and Hung Wai-shek.

180
00:08:17,760 --> 00:08:18,880
You didn't hear the racket?

181
00:08:19,040 --> 00:08:21,760
I always sleep with my headphone

182
00:08:21,880 --> 00:08:23,480
and I turned it on full blast.

183
00:08:23,560 --> 00:08:25,160
I really didn't hear anything.

184
00:08:26,880 --> 00:08:30,600
Brother Kin...Stop sleeping...
Get up...we're all set!

185
00:08:30,680 --> 00:08:32,440
We're done, Brother Kin...
Get up, Brother Kin...

186
00:08:32,520 --> 00:08:33,920
What game is this?

187
00:08:34,120 --> 00:08:34,920
It's not a game.

188
00:08:35,040 --> 00:08:36,640
We killed Ben.

189
00:08:36,800 --> 00:08:37,920
Seriously?

190
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:40,240
The body is downstairs. What now?

191
00:08:40,320 --> 00:08:41,200
I don't know.

192
00:08:41,320 --> 00:08:44,640
Suet, stay here. I'll go down
and check it out.

193
00:08:44,800 --> 00:08:45,280
Hurry...

194
00:08:45,400 --> 00:08:46,000
Hurry up, Brother Kin!

195
00:08:47,640 --> 00:08:51,280
What now? When we went downstairs,

196
00:08:51,400 --> 00:08:53,040
there wasn't so much blood...

197
00:08:53,160 --> 00:08:54,560
You rammed his head.

198
00:08:54,640 --> 00:08:57,200
I never actually saw Lau Yue-bun's body.

199
00:08:57,400 --> 00:08:58,800
If you were not involved in the killing

200
00:08:58,920 --> 00:08:59,840
and didn't know what happened,

201
00:08:59,920 --> 00:09:01,800
why did you go on the run with them?

202
00:09:01,920 --> 00:09:03,280
I didn't want to go.

203
00:09:03,440 --> 00:09:06,160
But they said it'll be dangerous for me
if I stayed.

204
00:09:06,240 --> 00:09:07,360
If the Police caught me,

205
00:09:07,480 --> 00:09:08,880
I won't be able to clear my name.

206
00:09:08,960 --> 00:09:11,120
We hid in a run-down guest house

207
00:09:11,200 --> 00:09:12,560
and dared not go out

208
00:09:12,680 --> 00:09:14,240
and we spent all our money.

209
00:09:14,400 --> 00:09:17,360
We're going to get busted

210
00:09:17,480 --> 00:09:19,040
and will be in jail for life.

211
00:09:19,120 --> 00:09:21,520
I don't want to go to jail.

212
00:09:24,560 --> 00:09:25,440
What now, Brother Kin?

213
00:09:25,720 --> 00:09:27,200
Turning ourselves in is better than
getting busted.

214
00:09:28,280 --> 00:09:29,360
We'll get a lighter sentence.

215
00:09:31,280 --> 00:09:34,480
Man up and face the music.

216
00:09:35,080 --> 00:09:36,640
They agreed to turn themselves in,

217
00:09:36,760 --> 00:09:38,240
but were dragging their feet.

218
00:09:38,360 --> 00:09:39,520
I couldn't take it any longer,

219
00:09:39,600 --> 00:09:41,280
so I snuck out and went to the Police.

220
00:09:41,680 --> 00:09:45,360
Witness, according to my client
Cheung Sai-chor,

221
00:09:45,440 --> 00:09:46,720
two days before the killing,

222
00:09:46,800 --> 00:09:49,440
did you and the three defendants
have a meeting to discuss

223
00:09:49,520 --> 00:09:50,640
how to kill the victim

224
00:09:50,720 --> 00:09:52,160
and how to get rid of the body?

225
00:09:53,520 --> 00:09:54,240
Yes.

226
00:09:54,480 --> 00:09:57,040
Forget the lesson, just kill him.

227
00:09:57,200 --> 00:09:59,280
Killing him is the easy part.

228
00:09:59,360 --> 00:10:00,880
What about the body?

229
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:03,360
Toss it into the Victoria Harbor.

230
00:10:03,480 --> 00:10:06,080
The sharks will get him.

231
00:10:06,800 --> 00:10:08,640
That's so boring.

232
00:10:08,760 --> 00:10:10,800
Don't you have any new ideas?

233
00:10:10,920 --> 00:10:12,320
I saw in a movie,

234
00:10:12,440 --> 00:10:15,360
they put the body in a crate

235
00:10:15,480 --> 00:10:18,080
and fill it up with cement.

236
00:10:18,160 --> 00:10:19,920
You won't see the body again.

237
00:10:20,320 --> 00:10:23,280
In the end, they used your idea

238
00:10:23,360 --> 00:10:25,840
and put the victim in a stone coffin.

239
00:10:25,920 --> 00:10:29,520
It wasn't my fault. I was just saying it.

240
00:10:29,640 --> 00:10:31,600
I didn't expect them to kill anyone.

241
00:10:31,720 --> 00:10:33,200
Why not?

242
00:10:33,360 --> 00:10:35,360
Because they always brag

243
00:10:35,480 --> 00:10:37,600
about murder and blackmail

244
00:10:37,720 --> 00:10:39,760
but they never actually did anything.

245
00:10:39,840 --> 00:10:42,800
How would I know they'd actually
kill the banker dude?

246
00:10:52,920 --> 00:10:55,520
You said you took no part in
handling the body.

247
00:10:55,880 --> 00:10:58,480
How come the Police found this
inside the stone coffin?

248
00:10:58,640 --> 00:11:00,000
Is this your press-on nail?

249
00:11:00,120 --> 00:11:02,400
No, I don't use press-on nails.

250
00:11:02,480 --> 00:11:04,400
You're the only female in the unit.

251
00:11:04,480 --> 00:11:06,400
Don't tell me this belongs to
the other defendants.

252
00:11:06,520 --> 00:11:10,240
I don't remember. I stopped using
gel nails a long time ago.

253
00:11:10,560 --> 00:11:13,760
Maybe Brother Kin brought other girls
to the unit and they dropped it.

254
00:11:13,840 --> 00:11:15,760
I don't know. Don't ask me.

255
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:17,760
I'd like to ask the witness something about

256
00:11:17,880 --> 00:11:19,920
the third defendant Tai Yat-kin.

257
00:11:20,080 --> 00:11:23,760
You and my client Hung Wai-shek and
the second defendant Cheung Sai-chor

258
00:11:23,880 --> 00:11:26,960
all admitted Tai Yat-kin said

259
00:11:27,080 --> 00:11:28,560
"just kill him".

260
00:11:29,120 --> 00:11:31,120
Does that mean killing Lau Yue-bun

261
00:11:31,200 --> 00:11:33,840
was Tai Yat-kin's idea, right?

262
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:35,680
Yes, Brother Kin did say that.

263
00:11:35,800 --> 00:11:37,520
But I'm sure he was just saying it.

264
00:11:37,640 --> 00:11:38,880
When he sobered up the next day,

265
00:11:38,960 --> 00:11:42,320
he made it clear to Dummy and Shek
he was just kidding.

266
00:11:42,400 --> 00:11:45,120
Then why didn't you tell the Police

267
00:11:45,280 --> 00:11:46,560
the first time you gave your statement?

268
00:11:46,680 --> 00:11:48,160
They didn't ask me.

269
00:11:48,280 --> 00:11:50,400
I'm telling you now because
you're asking me.

270
00:11:52,360 --> 00:11:54,880
We found a bank transfer record of him

271
00:11:54,960 --> 00:11:57,920
transferring money to you every month.

272
00:11:58,000 --> 00:11:59,120
Can you explain that?

273
00:11:59,200 --> 00:12:01,280
Brother Kin wanted me to be his secretary

274
00:12:01,400 --> 00:12:03,440
to help them jot down the minutes

275
00:12:03,560 --> 00:12:05,760
and he would pay me a monthly salary.

276
00:12:05,880 --> 00:12:09,040
You never took part in any of
their criminal acts.

277
00:12:09,160 --> 00:12:12,240
It was my client and the first defendant
Hung Wai-shek

278
00:12:12,320 --> 00:12:13,800
who actually did the work.

279
00:12:13,920 --> 00:12:15,600
How do you explain your pay

280
00:12:15,680 --> 00:12:17,760
is several times more than what they get?

281
00:12:18,200 --> 00:12:19,360
I don't know.

282
00:12:19,520 --> 00:12:20,800
Let me ask you more directly,

283
00:12:20,920 --> 00:12:22,560
what is your relationship with him?

284
00:12:22,680 --> 00:12:24,240
Objection, Your Honor.

285
00:12:24,360 --> 00:12:28,000
My client's relationship with the witness
is irrelevant to the case.

286
00:12:28,840 --> 00:12:29,920
Of course it is relevant.

287
00:12:30,080 --> 00:12:33,680
If the witness has an unusual relationship
with Tai Yat-kin,

288
00:12:33,760 --> 00:12:36,880
her testimony is unfair to my client.

289
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:38,160
Overruled.

290
00:12:39,480 --> 00:12:41,600
Witness, please answer the question.

291
00:12:41,720 --> 00:12:44,080
What is your relationship with Tai Yat-kin?

292
00:12:44,200 --> 00:12:45,040
Why are you protecting him?

293
00:12:45,160 --> 00:12:49,040
We're sworn brother and sister, that's all.

294
00:12:49,160 --> 00:12:51,440
And you sleep in the same bed?

295
00:12:51,560 --> 00:12:55,520
Yes, we do. But he never touched me.

296
00:12:55,720 --> 00:12:56,640
He never touched you.

297
00:12:56,760 --> 00:12:58,480
Does that mean he wanted to have
sex with you,

298
00:12:58,600 --> 00:12:59,360
but you turned him down?

299
00:12:59,440 --> 00:13:02,400
No. We don't fancy each other.

300
00:13:02,480 --> 00:13:04,640
So we didn't touch each other.

301
00:13:06,520 --> 00:13:09,760
It's true. I'm not casual in that regard.

302
00:13:09,840 --> 00:13:11,680
I don't even have a boyfriend.

303
00:13:11,800 --> 00:13:13,040
If that's the case,

304
00:13:13,120 --> 00:13:16,640
you should not sleep with a man
who's not your boyfriend, right?

305
00:13:24,440 --> 00:13:25,840
I hereby pronounce,

306
00:13:25,920 --> 00:13:28,080
the first defendant Hung Wai-shek,

307
00:13:28,160 --> 00:13:29,840
is not guilty of murder.

308
00:13:29,920 --> 00:13:31,200
but guilty of manslaughter.

309
00:13:31,320 --> 00:13:33,280
He is sentenced to life imprisonment.

310
00:13:33,640 --> 00:13:35,680
The second defendant Cheung Sai-chor,

311
00:13:35,840 --> 00:13:37,760
is not guilty of murder

312
00:13:37,840 --> 00:13:39,120
but guilty of manslaughter.

313
00:13:39,240 --> 00:13:41,040
He is sentenced to life imprisonment

314
00:13:41,120 --> 00:13:42,400
and remanded immediately.

315
00:13:42,840 --> 00:13:44,720
The third defendant Tai Yat-kin,

316
00:13:44,880 --> 00:13:47,520
is found not guilty of soliciting
to commit murder.

317
00:13:47,600 --> 00:13:50,560
But he helped the other defendants
in disposing the body,

318
00:13:50,640 --> 00:13:54,320
he's therefore guilty of preventing
the lawful burial of a body.

319
00:13:54,400 --> 00:13:56,160
He is sentenced to ten months' imprisonment.

320
00:13:56,560 --> 00:13:58,720
The immunized witness Ho Pui-suet,

321
00:13:58,800 --> 00:14:00,560
the circumstances of her crime are
relatively minor,

322
00:14:00,720 --> 00:14:03,440
considering her testimony against
the other defendants,

323
00:14:03,560 --> 00:14:06,320
charges against her are dropped and
she is hereby released by the court.

324
00:14:16,120 --> 00:14:18,080
I'm sorry, Shek.

325
00:14:18,200 --> 00:14:20,480
You have been so sweet to me,

326
00:14:20,840 --> 00:14:24,000
you think Brother Kin and I betrayed you?

327
00:14:24,160 --> 00:14:25,600
Of course not!

328
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:28,160
Maybe I really didn't hear Brother Kin

329
00:14:28,240 --> 00:14:31,120
telling us he was kidding when
he told us to kill Ben.

330
00:14:31,280 --> 00:14:33,840
You know me, I only listen half the time.

331
00:14:34,360 --> 00:14:36,480
Don't cry. It's not your fault.

332
00:14:38,280 --> 00:14:40,160
I can only blame my own stupidity

333
00:14:40,760 --> 00:14:42,400
for believing Brother Kin.

334
00:14:43,600 --> 00:14:48,000
Don't blame yourself. It's not your fault.

335
00:14:48,200 --> 00:14:50,080
Thanks for telling the court

336
00:14:50,200 --> 00:14:51,200
I took no part in killing Ben.

337
00:14:51,320 --> 00:14:54,720
That's why I was acquitted. Thanks.

338
00:14:55,400 --> 00:14:58,800
Just tell me if you need help with anything.

339
00:14:58,920 --> 00:15:03,040
Can you sell my phone and the game cards?

340
00:15:03,160 --> 00:15:05,520
Then give the money to my mother.

341
00:15:05,920 --> 00:15:08,240
I truly let her down.

342
00:15:09,600 --> 00:15:11,040
(Several months later)

343
00:15:11,360 --> 00:15:13,200
It's your favorite jasmine.

344
00:15:14,360 --> 00:15:15,680
Can you smell that?

345
00:15:16,920 --> 00:15:17,680
Cathy?

346
00:15:19,240 --> 00:15:20,000
Ben?

347
00:15:23,240 --> 00:15:25,040
Cathy, you're awake!

348
00:15:25,160 --> 00:15:26,400
I'll get Dr. Chung!

349
00:15:26,600 --> 00:15:27,520
Dr. Chung...

350
00:15:28,320 --> 00:15:31,200
Cathy, you were in a coma for a few months.

351
00:15:31,280 --> 00:15:33,680
You fell down the stairs.

352
00:15:33,800 --> 00:15:36,240
You hit your head and had a concussion.

353
00:15:41,160 --> 00:15:44,080
I checked, the fracture on your leg

354
00:15:44,160 --> 00:15:45,760
hasn't completely recovered.

355
00:15:45,920 --> 00:15:50,000
You'll need practice before
you can walk again.

356
00:15:50,120 --> 00:15:51,440
But don't worry too much.

357
00:15:51,600 --> 00:15:53,920
The key is to get enough rest.

358
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:56,160
If you need anything, just let us know, OK?

359
00:15:57,400 --> 00:15:58,400
Get some rest.

360
00:16:03,240 --> 00:16:04,160
Tracy!

361
00:16:05,880 --> 00:16:07,360
I know what you're going to ask.

362
00:16:10,360 --> 00:16:11,680
The baby is gone.

363
00:16:36,960 --> 00:16:40,480
Thanks. You and the others
for taking care of me.

364
00:16:41,040 --> 00:16:43,520
Don't be silly. You always took care of us.

365
00:16:43,640 --> 00:16:46,240
You're alone and have no family.

366
00:16:46,320 --> 00:16:48,040
It's sad to be in a hospital.

367
00:16:48,120 --> 00:16:49,640
We'll all keep an eye on you.

368
00:16:51,800 --> 00:16:55,280
By the way, who sent the flowers?

369
00:16:55,640 --> 00:16:56,560
Mary did.

370
00:16:56,880 --> 00:16:57,920
When you were in a coma,

371
00:16:58,040 --> 00:17:00,480
she often asked me to take her in
a wheelchair to visit you.

372
00:17:00,560 --> 00:17:02,360
When the flowers have wilted,

373
00:17:02,560 --> 00:17:04,440
she'd urge me to buy fresh ones.

374
00:17:05,600 --> 00:17:07,280
I want to see her.

375
00:17:07,400 --> 00:17:10,720
You just woke up. You should stay in bed.

376
00:17:11,200 --> 00:17:13,600
You know seeing me will make her better.

377
00:17:14,080 --> 00:17:16,560
Come on, get me a wheelchair.

378
00:17:17,360 --> 00:17:19,680
OK...I get it for you.

379
00:17:25,920 --> 00:17:28,400
Mary has been in the rehab room
a lot lately.

380
00:17:28,480 --> 00:17:30,840
She must really want to walk again.

381
00:17:31,200 --> 00:17:33,200
She's been practicing hard.

382
00:17:34,560 --> 00:17:35,680
Take it easy.

383
00:17:40,880 --> 00:17:43,840
Slowly...small steps.

384
00:17:47,280 --> 00:17:50,080
I quit. I'm a loser.

385
00:17:50,200 --> 00:17:51,440
What's the point of practicing?

386
00:17:51,520 --> 00:17:53,600
This is unnecessary. Why bother?

387
00:17:53,840 --> 00:17:56,160
You only practiced for a minute last time...

388
00:17:56,440 --> 00:17:58,240
Let me go in by myself...
Today, you've been up for five minutes...

389
00:17:58,320 --> 00:17:59,360
I don't want to impose on you.

390
00:17:59,440 --> 00:18:00,600
You should get back to work.
You can do it next time.

391
00:18:00,720 --> 00:18:01,280
OK!

392
00:18:01,440 --> 00:18:03,120
Have a nice chat.
I can't do this...

393
00:18:03,240 --> 00:18:04,320
She is different when she's around you.

394
00:18:04,440 --> 00:18:05,120
Let me go back to my room.

395
00:18:05,240 --> 00:18:06,000
Thanks.

396
00:18:06,880 --> 00:18:08,720
Let me go back to my room, OK?

397
00:18:08,800 --> 00:18:09,760
OK...

398
00:18:14,360 --> 00:18:15,040
Mary!

399
00:18:16,680 --> 00:18:20,400
Cathy?! You woke up! You finally woke up!

400
00:18:20,560 --> 00:18:23,120
Are you OK? You scared me to death!

401
00:18:23,200 --> 00:18:24,320
I'm fine.

402
00:18:24,480 --> 00:18:28,880
I've been asking Heaven the whole time
why am I being punished?

403
00:18:28,960 --> 00:18:30,560
What have I done wrong?

404
00:18:31,160 --> 00:18:33,640
Not only am I plagued with this rare disease

405
00:18:33,720 --> 00:18:37,840
they also took from me
the two kindest people I know.

406
00:18:38,320 --> 00:18:41,560
I kept praying to Heaven to let me
trade with you.

407
00:18:41,920 --> 00:18:43,920
I'd rather die than watch you die.

408
00:18:44,040 --> 00:18:45,360
Do you understand?

409
00:18:45,480 --> 00:18:49,200
Your prayers have been answered.

410
00:18:49,600 --> 00:18:50,400
Did you know

411
00:18:50,480 --> 00:18:55,320
I woke up because I smelled
the jasmine you brought me.

412
00:18:55,400 --> 00:18:58,240
You gave me strength. Thank you.

413
00:18:59,280 --> 00:19:00,640
Ben was a fool.

414
00:19:01,960 --> 00:19:06,040
He risked his life to make money
for a loser like me.

415
00:19:07,200 --> 00:19:12,000
It was my fault. I'm so sorry...

416
00:19:12,080 --> 00:19:15,920
No, I should be sorry.

417
00:19:17,920 --> 00:19:20,360
Ben was anxious to make money

418
00:19:20,920 --> 00:19:22,480
not just for you...

419
00:19:25,160 --> 00:19:27,320
but also for our baby.

420
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:32,640
The nurse told me you had a miscarriage.

421
00:19:32,840 --> 00:19:34,800
I thought I heard her wrong.

422
00:19:35,640 --> 00:19:38,840
Trust me...I never intended

423
00:19:38,920 --> 00:19:40,800
to use the baby to take Ben away.

424
00:19:40,960 --> 00:19:41,920
I was selfish...
Don't...

425
00:19:42,040 --> 00:19:43,440
I can't bear to have an abortion...

426
00:19:43,560 --> 00:19:46,040
If you two decided to abandon me,

427
00:19:46,160 --> 00:19:48,040
none of this would have happened.

428
00:19:48,960 --> 00:19:50,160
Now that Ben is dead,

429
00:19:50,320 --> 00:19:51,440
we are no longer connected.

430
00:19:51,560 --> 00:19:53,280
You need not look after me anymore.

431
00:19:53,640 --> 00:19:56,520
It's a nurse's duty to look after
her patients.

432
00:19:57,320 --> 00:20:00,080
I chose this profession because I like it.

433
00:20:01,240 --> 00:20:04,320
When we met, I didn't even know Ben.

434
00:20:04,680 --> 00:20:06,640
I truly want what's best for you,

435
00:20:06,800 --> 00:20:08,520
that's why I encouraged you

436
00:20:08,640 --> 00:20:10,480
and took care of you.

437
00:20:11,920 --> 00:20:14,720
I know you want to.

438
00:20:14,800 --> 00:20:18,720
But I don't want to become a burden to you.

439
00:20:19,480 --> 00:20:23,440
Ben liked jasmine because I like jasmine.

440
00:20:23,960 --> 00:20:25,800
He gave you jasmine

441
00:20:26,160 --> 00:20:28,960
and inadvertently gave away
our relationship.

442
00:20:29,120 --> 00:20:30,720
When I was in a coma,

443
00:20:31,720 --> 00:20:33,520
the smell of the jasmine you brought me

444
00:20:33,640 --> 00:20:35,360
was the reason I woke up.

445
00:20:36,560 --> 00:20:38,360
Don't you find it amazing?

446
00:20:40,160 --> 00:20:41,920
Do you know why I like jasmine?

447
00:20:43,760 --> 00:20:47,520
Its floriography is "you are my life".

448
00:20:50,240 --> 00:20:56,720
You, me and Ben are destined to have

449
00:20:56,880 --> 00:21:00,880
an important place in each other's lives.

450
00:21:01,880 --> 00:21:04,960
That's why, with or without Ben,

451
00:21:05,040 --> 00:21:07,800
you and I will move on with
our lives together.

452
00:21:14,920 --> 00:21:18,280
The physiatrist said you're making
good progress.

453
00:21:22,080 --> 00:21:23,200
See?

454
00:21:25,120 --> 00:21:27,680
I'll soon join you in rehab.

455
00:21:28,120 --> 00:21:31,640
You have no family, I'm all alone.

456
00:21:33,080 --> 00:21:36,640
We'll support each other, OK?

457
00:21:37,200 --> 00:21:39,600
Let's stop apologizing

458
00:21:39,800 --> 00:21:41,920
and don't bring up the word "burden", OK?

459
00:22:22,400 --> 00:22:25,920
Where are you? I need to talk to you.

460
00:22:26,400 --> 00:22:28,520
I'll be home once I wrap things up.

461
00:22:33,840 --> 00:22:35,920
Tai Yat-kin got ten months.

462
00:22:36,080 --> 00:22:38,640
(Prettiest witness in stone coffin case)

463
00:22:40,160 --> 00:22:44,080
Ho Pui-suet, the immunized witness
was acquitted?

464
00:22:46,080 --> 00:22:48,400
Sorry about calling you so late.

465
00:22:48,520 --> 00:22:50,160
I have something to ask you.

466
00:22:50,640 --> 00:22:53,800
Gogo Sir, I read the certified copy
of the trial.

467
00:22:53,920 --> 00:22:54,960
None of the defendants

468
00:22:55,040 --> 00:22:56,960
said anything about Ben's phone.

469
00:22:57,160 --> 00:22:59,360
That's because we couldn't find the phone

470
00:22:59,480 --> 00:23:01,760
on Mr. Lau, in his car or at the
scene of the crime.

471
00:23:01,920 --> 00:23:02,960
The two killers said

472
00:23:03,040 --> 00:23:04,840
Ben's car was blocking another car.

473
00:23:04,920 --> 00:23:06,400
The owner of the car called him

474
00:23:06,480 --> 00:23:08,400
and the killers went downstairs to move it.

475
00:23:08,480 --> 00:23:10,640
That means they should have kept the phone.

476
00:23:10,800 --> 00:23:12,400
Maybe after they killed Mr. Lau,

477
00:23:12,560 --> 00:23:14,320
they didn't want anyone to find him,

478
00:23:14,400 --> 00:23:17,200
so they ripped apart the phone
and tossed it.

479
00:23:17,280 --> 00:23:19,680
Normally, they admitted everything else,

480
00:23:19,760 --> 00:23:21,080
they should admit this part as well.

481
00:23:21,200 --> 00:23:23,520
Exactly! Don't you find that rather odd?

482
00:23:23,760 --> 00:23:27,440
Also, Tai Yat-kin was only convicted of

483
00:23:27,520 --> 00:23:29,560
"preventing the legal burial of a body".

484
00:23:29,640 --> 00:23:31,440
I think there should be more to it.

485
00:23:31,640 --> 00:23:32,400
Why?

486
00:23:32,520 --> 00:23:35,600
Because I saw Ben got into
a fierce argument with him.

487
00:23:35,720 --> 00:23:37,840
That was the last time I saw him.

488
00:23:37,960 --> 00:23:38,960
We agreed on a 50/50 split.

489
00:23:39,040 --> 00:23:40,400
The money is not enough.

490
00:23:40,560 --> 00:23:41,680
Did you take my share?

491
00:23:42,200 --> 00:23:46,280
$2M is not enough? You're too greedy.

492
00:23:46,400 --> 00:23:47,320
What have you done?

493
00:23:47,440 --> 00:23:48,800
You're just the go-between.

494
00:23:48,920 --> 00:23:50,560
I did all the dirty work.

495
00:23:50,720 --> 00:23:52,840
If things should go south, I'll go to jail.

496
00:23:52,960 --> 00:23:54,400
I want $500K more.

497
00:23:55,240 --> 00:23:56,800
The Boss trusts me.

498
00:23:56,880 --> 00:23:57,920
If I didn't hook you up,

499
00:23:58,120 --> 00:24:00,520
you won't see the money.

500
00:24:00,800 --> 00:24:02,320
You should know who's calling the shots.

501
00:24:02,480 --> 00:24:04,800
Fine! Get someone else to do it.

502
00:24:04,920 --> 00:24:06,720
I won't take the next order.

503
00:24:06,840 --> 00:24:08,640
Let's see how you explain to the Boss.

504
00:24:08,800 --> 00:24:12,120
Listen, it's too late to back out now.

505
00:24:12,200 --> 00:24:14,120
You want to quit? You won't get away.

506
00:24:14,280 --> 00:24:15,680
I'll kill you if you quit.

507
00:24:16,960 --> 00:24:19,440
He threatened to kill Ben.

508
00:24:19,600 --> 00:24:20,720
I think he had a hand in it.

509
00:24:20,880 --> 00:24:22,400
He might even be the mastermind.

510
00:24:22,560 --> 00:24:26,480
Also, how could Ho Pui-suet be acquitted?

511
00:24:26,560 --> 00:24:28,360
Because she was the immunized witness.

512
00:24:28,480 --> 00:24:31,080
I know. But have you read her statement?

513
00:24:31,160 --> 00:24:33,120
I think she was hiding something.

514
00:24:33,200 --> 00:24:36,560
She said she has a platonic relationship
with Tai Yat-kin,

515
00:24:36,640 --> 00:24:38,880
But I can tell you I have seen her before.

516
00:24:39,040 --> 00:24:41,320
She told me she's on the pill.

517
00:24:41,400 --> 00:24:43,080
Is it possible you're pregnant?

518
00:24:43,200 --> 00:24:44,360
Of course not!

519
00:24:44,440 --> 00:24:46,600
I'm on the pill. I don't have a baby.

520
00:24:46,680 --> 00:24:48,280
There are so many questionable points.

521
00:24:48,360 --> 00:24:50,040
You should re-start the investigation.

522
00:24:50,120 --> 00:24:51,120
I'm not saying you're wrong.

523
00:24:51,200 --> 00:24:53,120
But the Police work with evidence.

524
00:24:53,200 --> 00:24:55,120
You can't possibly ignore
these questionable points.

525
00:24:55,200 --> 00:24:56,720
No, but you must understand,

526
00:24:56,800 --> 00:24:58,000
the case is a closed file.

527
00:24:58,080 --> 00:25:00,040
Also, you should know no one
can be charged for the same offense twice,

528
00:25:00,120 --> 00:25:01,360
unless there's new evidence.

529
00:25:01,480 --> 00:25:03,520
But the things you said are not evidence.

530
00:25:03,640 --> 00:25:05,200
They're merely your speculation.

531
00:25:07,600 --> 00:25:09,800
Why take the pill if there's no guy...

532
00:25:10,320 --> 00:25:12,760
Let's take a picture next to the nice logo.

533
00:25:12,880 --> 00:25:13,560
Great!

534
00:25:14,120 --> 00:25:14,800
Yeah...

535
00:25:14,920 --> 00:25:17,840
Folks, I brought a friend.

536
00:25:20,480 --> 00:25:21,120
Come...

537
00:25:21,240 --> 00:25:22,760
New friend?
Sit down...

538
00:25:22,840 --> 00:25:23,920
Nice...
Of course!

539
00:25:24,040 --> 00:25:26,880
From the stone coffin case?
Sit...

540
00:25:27,000 --> 00:25:29,200
You're so much prettier in person.

541
00:25:29,320 --> 00:25:30,560
Stop teasing me.

542
00:25:30,640 --> 00:25:32,560
The reporters won't care how I look.

543
00:25:32,640 --> 00:25:34,040
They made my face as big as a pan!

544
00:25:34,160 --> 00:25:37,360
They say you're working as a part-time
girlfriend right now.

545
00:25:37,480 --> 00:25:38,400
Is that true?

546
00:25:38,520 --> 00:25:40,640
No! I don't do that.

547
00:25:40,800 --> 00:25:43,640
You have Instabook? I want to follow you.

548
00:25:43,760 --> 00:25:44,800
Sure!
Me too.

549
00:25:44,880 --> 00:25:45,840
Here...

550
00:25:57,880 --> 00:26:01,360
Let's go...
Ten...Nothing...

551
00:26:06,520 --> 00:26:09,200
Why are you phubbing over here?

552
00:26:09,360 --> 00:26:10,400
Drink this.

553
00:26:11,720 --> 00:26:13,880
I heard you're living with Bing, right?

554
00:26:15,000 --> 00:26:17,520
I said...how do you like living with Bing?

555
00:26:17,600 --> 00:26:19,200
Yes.

556
00:26:19,280 --> 00:26:21,680
But sometimes when her boyfriend
sleeps over,

557
00:26:21,800 --> 00:26:23,440
it's not too convenient.

558
00:26:23,560 --> 00:26:26,640
Why don't you stay with me? I live alone.

559
00:26:26,760 --> 00:26:28,480
I can't do that.

560
00:26:28,600 --> 00:26:29,920
We're friends, right?

561
00:26:30,080 --> 00:26:31,800
Don't argue. It's settled, OK?

562
00:26:31,920 --> 00:26:34,240
Let me think about it. Thanks.

563
00:26:37,520 --> 00:26:39,360
I want to buy your bag.

564
00:26:39,440 --> 00:26:40,600
Where should we meet up?

565
00:26:40,960 --> 00:26:42,720
Let's meet in Tsimshatsui East.

566
00:26:42,800 --> 00:26:45,920
Nurse Tse, it's you!?

567
00:26:46,080 --> 00:26:48,880
This is my first time on Comesaround.

568
00:26:49,000 --> 00:26:50,880
But I spotted your bag right away.

569
00:26:50,960 --> 00:26:53,360
I guess it's destiny.

570
00:26:53,720 --> 00:26:55,360
Yes. Please check.

571
00:26:55,720 --> 00:26:56,760
The bag is practically new.

572
00:26:56,840 --> 00:26:58,400
I only used it a few times.

573
00:26:58,520 --> 00:27:01,600
I'm only selling because I need the money.

574
00:27:02,320 --> 00:27:05,200
This is nice. Let me try it.

575
00:27:06,160 --> 00:27:06,960
How do I look?

576
00:27:07,480 --> 00:27:09,600
It doesn't quite go with your style.

577
00:27:09,680 --> 00:27:12,880
I want to try different styles.

578
00:27:13,040 --> 00:27:15,640
Is this the girl band style?

579
00:27:15,760 --> 00:27:17,360
Y2K.

580
00:27:17,840 --> 00:27:22,840
You have Y2K clothes, skirts or shoes?

581
00:27:22,920 --> 00:27:23,800
I'm OK with those.

582
00:27:23,880 --> 00:27:24,760
You can sell them to me directly.

583
00:27:24,880 --> 00:27:26,240
Save me the trouble of looking around.

584
00:27:34,800 --> 00:27:36,960
When did they open the gel nail shop?

585
00:27:37,040 --> 00:27:38,160
You want?

586
00:27:38,360 --> 00:27:40,400
I always wanted to try.

587
00:27:42,560 --> 00:27:44,400
What about you? You do nails?

588
00:27:44,560 --> 00:27:46,800
I love it. But haven't done it in a while.

589
00:27:48,760 --> 00:27:51,360
$400?! That's expensive.

590
00:27:51,520 --> 00:27:54,280
Don't do it here. I can do it for you.

591
00:27:54,360 --> 00:27:55,360
You know how?

592
00:27:55,800 --> 00:27:56,400
Great!

593
00:27:57,000 --> 00:27:59,560
This way is better for your nails.

594
00:27:59,640 --> 00:28:01,360
I have done gel nails for too long,

595
00:28:01,520 --> 00:28:03,320
that's why they break and chip easily.

596
00:28:03,880 --> 00:28:04,960
What would you like?

597
00:28:06,120 --> 00:28:08,600
Anything. I trust your taste.

598
00:28:10,160 --> 00:28:11,920
There's something I want to say,

599
00:28:12,000 --> 00:28:13,080
I hope you won't mind.

600
00:28:13,200 --> 00:28:14,040
What?

601
00:28:14,160 --> 00:28:16,120
When I bought your bag,

602
00:28:16,200 --> 00:28:18,360
I recognized you from the stone coffin case.

603
00:28:18,480 --> 00:28:19,760
I'm not sure if you want to bring it up,

604
00:28:19,880 --> 00:28:21,200
so I didn't say anything.

605
00:28:21,360 --> 00:28:23,560
My face was posted everywhere

606
00:28:23,640 --> 00:28:25,360
and people criticized me.

607
00:28:25,520 --> 00:28:26,880
It's impossible not to recognize me.

608
00:28:27,080 --> 00:28:28,880
Don't worry! I don't believe those people.

609
00:28:29,000 --> 00:28:30,400
I only believe in what I see.

610
00:28:30,560 --> 00:28:32,400
The time we have spent together,

611
00:28:32,600 --> 00:28:35,360
I found you quite simple-minded.

612
00:28:36,400 --> 00:28:38,360
You're the first person who took my side.

613
00:28:38,480 --> 00:28:40,040
Since the case came to light,

614
00:28:40,160 --> 00:28:43,120
people didn't seem to mind,

615
00:28:43,240 --> 00:28:46,000
but I know deep down they're afraid of me.

616
00:28:46,520 --> 00:28:48,280
Brother Kin is not around,

617
00:28:48,440 --> 00:28:50,120
I don't know who I can go to.

618
00:28:50,640 --> 00:28:53,280
Brother Kin? The guy who's been nice to you?

619
00:28:53,360 --> 00:28:55,080
Are you quite close?

620
00:28:55,160 --> 00:28:56,880
You'll do anything he says?

621
00:28:57,000 --> 00:28:59,120
Yes. I'll do anything for him.

622
00:28:59,240 --> 00:29:02,960
One time, Dummy and Shek
bought chloroform,

623
00:29:03,040 --> 00:29:04,960
I didn't know it stinks.

624
00:29:05,080 --> 00:29:07,360
Brother Kin told me to smell it, so I did.

625
00:29:07,480 --> 00:29:10,160
I felt so dizzy afterwards.

626
00:29:10,440 --> 00:29:12,400
Tai Yat-kin tells you to say nothing,
you keep your mouth shut.

627
00:29:12,560 --> 00:29:16,080
If he tells you to hide evidence,
you'll do it too.

628
00:29:16,200 --> 00:29:17,120
Done!

629
00:29:19,320 --> 00:29:20,400
It's nice!

630
00:29:21,000 --> 00:29:23,800
Cathy, I need your opinion on something.

631
00:29:24,640 --> 00:29:26,560
I met a guy at a bar...

632
00:29:26,640 --> 00:29:28,640
He asked me to live with him.

633
00:29:28,760 --> 00:29:30,960
You think I should?

634
00:29:31,080 --> 00:29:33,200
It's not the first time you live with a guy.

635
00:29:33,320 --> 00:29:35,280
Go ahead if you trust him.

636
00:29:35,760 --> 00:29:36,400
OK!

637
00:29:39,120 --> 00:29:42,840
Gogo Sir, Ho Pui-suet did
these nails for me.

638
00:29:43,000 --> 00:29:43,880
Don't you think the pattern

639
00:29:43,960 --> 00:29:46,640
is identical to the nail found inside
the stone coffin?

640
00:29:46,760 --> 00:29:49,560
That means she took part in
handling the body.

641
00:29:49,640 --> 00:29:50,960
Shouldn't you bring her in for questioning?

642
00:29:51,120 --> 00:29:53,520
Unlike fingernails, press-on nails
have no DNA.

643
00:29:54,160 --> 00:29:57,080
The pattern is similar, but you can't prove

644
00:29:57,160 --> 00:29:58,280
the nail found inside the stone coffin

645
00:29:58,400 --> 00:29:59,360
belonged to Ho Pui-suet.

646
00:29:59,440 --> 00:30:02,400
At least you think they're similar.

647
00:30:04,400 --> 00:30:05,680
The Chief is calling a meeting.

648
00:30:05,760 --> 00:30:06,360
OK!

649
00:30:06,440 --> 00:30:07,520
Hey, come here.

650
00:30:08,440 --> 00:30:10,040
Look at Miss Tse's nails.

651
00:30:10,120 --> 00:30:12,560
Are they similar to the one found
inside the stone coffin?

652
00:30:12,960 --> 00:30:14,640
They're similar.

653
00:30:14,800 --> 00:30:18,360
But that one had whiskers, this one doesn't.

654
00:30:18,600 --> 00:30:19,600
They're not the same.

655
00:30:19,720 --> 00:30:21,560
At least he thinks they're similar.

656
00:30:21,640 --> 00:30:22,840
Unlike machines,

657
00:30:22,960 --> 00:30:24,720
humans don't draw the exact same thing.

658
00:30:24,800 --> 00:30:25,920
Anyone who walks in here

659
00:30:26,040 --> 00:30:28,160
can refute your so-called evidence.

660
00:30:30,800 --> 00:30:31,920
It comes off so easily,

661
00:30:32,080 --> 00:30:34,960
even if the nail in the coffin
belonged to Ho Pui-suet,

662
00:30:35,200 --> 00:30:39,040
it's also possible it fell out beforehand,

663
00:30:39,120 --> 00:30:41,120
when those two were preparing the cement,

664
00:30:41,240 --> 00:30:42,640
it got stuck somehow.

665
00:30:42,760 --> 00:30:44,720
Are you sure you're not overthinking?

666
00:30:51,080 --> 00:30:54,240
Sorry. Something came up. I need to go.

667
00:30:55,160 --> 00:30:57,680
Suet...

668
00:31:00,680 --> 00:31:02,280
What happened?

669
00:31:02,360 --> 00:31:04,400
That guy I met earlier on...

670
00:31:04,560 --> 00:31:07,560
I went to his place after happy hour.

671
00:31:07,880 --> 00:31:09,360
He wanted to mess with me

672
00:31:09,480 --> 00:31:11,120
and climbed on top...

673
00:31:11,200 --> 00:31:12,960
I had to fight to get away...

674
00:31:13,120 --> 00:31:14,080
You moved in with him?

675
00:31:14,160 --> 00:31:15,440
I asked you last time,

676
00:31:15,520 --> 00:31:16,800
you said if he's a nice guy,

677
00:31:16,880 --> 00:31:18,640
I can move in with him.

678
00:31:18,800 --> 00:31:21,320
I didn't know he was a creep.

679
00:31:21,840 --> 00:31:22,800
Now I'm really scared.

680
00:31:22,880 --> 00:31:25,440
I don't know who else to call.

681
00:31:25,560 --> 00:31:26,400
Don't worry!

682
00:31:27,560 --> 00:31:28,880
You came to the right person.

683
00:31:29,240 --> 00:31:29,840
Come on...

684
00:31:37,920 --> 00:31:39,760
Scumbag!

685
00:31:40,840 --> 00:31:41,360
Let's go!

686
00:32:06,120 --> 00:32:08,600
Don't be so gullible.

687
00:32:08,720 --> 00:32:10,360
You must learn to protect yourself, OK?

688
00:32:10,640 --> 00:32:12,640
I thought that creep would be like
Brother Kin

689
00:32:12,720 --> 00:32:15,040
who felt sorry for me and took me in

690
00:32:15,160 --> 00:32:16,880
and looked after me like a sister.

691
00:32:16,960 --> 00:32:19,080
You're the only person I trust now.

692
00:32:19,400 --> 00:32:20,400
You're so simple minded,

693
00:32:20,560 --> 00:32:22,120
it's dangerous to be out there alone.

694
00:32:22,200 --> 00:32:23,440
You should go home.

695
00:32:24,040 --> 00:32:25,360
I don't have a home.

696
00:32:25,960 --> 00:32:27,000
You don't?

697
00:32:28,040 --> 00:32:29,520
When I was little,

698
00:32:29,600 --> 00:32:32,400
Mom ran away with another man.

699
00:32:32,520 --> 00:32:34,800
My old man was so pissed,

700
00:32:34,960 --> 00:32:38,280
he used to hit me when he's upset.

701
00:32:38,400 --> 00:32:40,640
Then he married another woman

702
00:32:40,840 --> 00:32:42,880
who gave him a son.

703
00:32:43,000 --> 00:32:45,600
The mother and son bullied me

704
00:32:46,880 --> 00:32:49,440
and my old man never once defended me.

705
00:32:50,120 --> 00:32:53,080
They're family, not me.

706
00:32:54,040 --> 00:32:56,880
That's why I left.

707
00:32:57,600 --> 00:32:59,200
I didn't even finish high school.

708
00:32:59,320 --> 00:33:00,400
I know nothing.

709
00:33:00,720 --> 00:33:02,600
Someone like me,

710
00:33:02,680 --> 00:33:03,360
if I don't sponge off someone else,

711
00:33:03,480 --> 00:33:04,800
how could I survive?

712
00:33:06,440 --> 00:33:10,160
I can only blame myself for
being a bad judge of character.

713
00:33:11,160 --> 00:33:14,080
Brother Kin was right about me, I'm stupid.

714
00:33:15,000 --> 00:33:17,840
Hey! Don't say that.

715
00:33:18,040 --> 00:33:20,640
Thanks for saving me just now.

716
00:33:21,080 --> 00:33:23,600
If only you could have saved me last time.

717
00:33:23,680 --> 00:33:24,760
Last time?

718
00:33:24,880 --> 00:33:27,440
Yes! Remember I ran into you outside
the industrial building,

719
00:33:27,640 --> 00:33:29,240
I stopped you on the street?

720
00:33:29,320 --> 00:33:30,880
I didn't really want to pay you back.

721
00:33:31,000 --> 00:33:32,960
Suet, it's time.

722
00:33:33,080 --> 00:33:35,160
Go on ahead. I'll catch up.

723
00:33:36,440 --> 00:33:37,040
Can you...

724
00:33:37,160 --> 00:33:38,240
Suet, what's holding you up?

725
00:33:38,320 --> 00:33:39,880
We have a plane to catch!

726
00:33:40,000 --> 00:33:40,480
What?

727
00:33:40,600 --> 00:33:42,080
Bye! Hurry...

728
00:33:42,200 --> 00:33:44,280
You didn't want to go away with them.

729
00:33:44,880 --> 00:33:48,320
When we first met, you took me to a doctor,

730
00:33:48,440 --> 00:33:49,920
and loaned me money,

731
00:33:50,160 --> 00:33:51,920
I knew you're a good person.

732
00:33:52,920 --> 00:33:54,960
I was hoping you could help me ditch them.

733
00:33:55,120 --> 00:33:57,360
It's over now. Let's forget it.

734
00:33:57,520 --> 00:33:59,760
If you have nowhere to go,

735
00:33:59,960 --> 00:34:02,200
would you like to stay?

736
00:34:02,320 --> 00:34:03,360
You can sleep on the sofa.

737
00:34:03,560 --> 00:34:05,800
Really? Thanks!

738
00:34:15,240 --> 00:34:16,200
You're not feeling well?

739
00:34:17,960 --> 00:34:20,000
No. I'm taking birth control pills.

740
00:34:20,160 --> 00:34:22,320
But you said you're not with anyone.

741
00:34:22,440 --> 00:34:23,760
Why do you need the pill?

742
00:34:23,920 --> 00:34:26,160
The doctor prescribed them for my acne.

743
00:34:26,280 --> 00:34:28,240
It can regulate my hormones.

744
00:34:28,400 --> 00:34:29,440
That's right!

745
00:34:31,640 --> 00:34:33,520
The pill has the effect.

746
00:34:33,600 --> 00:34:34,720
Why didn't I think of that?

747
00:34:34,840 --> 00:34:35,680
What did you say?

748
00:34:35,920 --> 00:34:36,960
Nothing!

749
00:34:38,200 --> 00:34:39,360
Here you go...

750
00:34:41,520 --> 00:34:42,200
Wow?

751
00:34:43,760 --> 00:34:44,400
What?

752
00:34:44,560 --> 00:34:46,880
Your bracelet is really nice.

753
00:34:47,040 --> 00:34:49,040
Let me help you...OK!

754
00:34:49,200 --> 00:34:50,000
Thanks.

755
00:34:50,800 --> 00:34:53,520
Good night.
Good night.

756
00:34:57,200 --> 00:34:58,480
You're up?

757
00:34:58,760 --> 00:35:01,280
Sit down and have some breakfast.

758
00:35:03,960 --> 00:35:06,560
Wow! What's with you today?

759
00:35:06,720 --> 00:35:09,920
I didn't know you're a breakfast person.

760
00:35:10,400 --> 00:35:12,160
I don't usually get up this early.

761
00:35:12,240 --> 00:35:13,440
But I want to be with you.

762
00:35:13,560 --> 00:35:15,640
I think eating breakfast with someone

763
00:35:15,720 --> 00:35:17,200
is a very happy thing.

764
00:35:17,320 --> 00:35:19,280
Really? I think so too.

765
00:35:19,360 --> 00:35:20,480
Hurry up and try this.

766
00:35:20,600 --> 00:35:22,880
OK, I'll try your cooking.

767
00:35:26,200 --> 00:35:27,840
All set.

768
00:35:28,160 --> 00:35:32,720
Not bad at all. You're really quite good.

769
00:35:32,800 --> 00:35:35,040
Only because you have nice skin.

770
00:35:35,160 --> 00:35:37,640
You're too busy to put on makeup.

771
00:35:38,840 --> 00:35:43,640
Unlike me, this is the only thing I know.

772
00:35:44,320 --> 00:35:46,800
If one can find something one is good at,

773
00:35:46,960 --> 00:35:48,800
it's already something quite commendable.

774
00:35:48,960 --> 00:35:51,440
You're the first person to
say that about me.

775
00:35:51,640 --> 00:35:55,520
I think you can pursue a career
in makeup or styling.

776
00:35:55,600 --> 00:35:57,280
Maybe this is your calling.

777
00:36:04,920 --> 00:36:05,920
Suet?

778
00:36:06,120 --> 00:36:07,720
I had a nightmare.

779
00:36:07,800 --> 00:36:09,600
I need to sleep with someone.

780
00:36:16,760 --> 00:36:17,520
Suet?

781
00:36:18,840 --> 00:36:21,360
I always sleep with my headphone

782
00:36:21,480 --> 00:36:23,040
and I turned it on full blast.

783
00:36:23,160 --> 00:36:24,880
I really didn't hear anything.

784
00:36:27,400 --> 00:36:29,240
Just like a kid.

785
00:36:35,520 --> 00:36:37,280
Are you tired from work?

786
00:36:37,640 --> 00:36:39,280
Everyone gets tired from work.

787
00:36:40,120 --> 00:36:41,520
I may be tired,

788
00:36:42,080 --> 00:36:46,400
but I haven't felt so good
in a long time.

789
00:36:46,560 --> 00:36:48,320
Is it because of the sea?

790
00:36:48,520 --> 00:36:49,640
Every time I'm at the seaside,

791
00:36:49,720 --> 00:36:50,960
I felt really good

792
00:36:51,080 --> 00:36:52,880
as if my troubles went away.

793
00:36:58,800 --> 00:36:59,720
What are you doing?

794
00:37:01,400 --> 00:37:02,960
Cathy, this is for you.

795
00:37:03,040 --> 00:37:04,160
This?

796
00:37:04,600 --> 00:37:06,480
Thanks for taking me in.

797
00:37:06,920 --> 00:37:09,520
My boyfriend liked instant photography.

798
00:37:09,640 --> 00:37:11,520
Why would someone young like you
like something so old fashioned?

799
00:37:11,680 --> 00:37:13,760
Age has nothing to do with it.

800
00:37:13,880 --> 00:37:16,160
You never know what you captured.

801
00:37:16,240 --> 00:37:17,760
I like the surprise.

802
00:37:18,680 --> 00:37:21,040
Hey...you'll make me look ugly.

803
00:37:21,160 --> 00:37:23,440
You said you like the surprise.

804
00:37:24,520 --> 00:37:26,480
My ex said the exact same thing.

805
00:37:26,600 --> 00:37:28,000
Maybe you two think alike.

806
00:37:29,080 --> 00:37:32,000
I should call you Auntie Suet.

807
00:37:32,120 --> 00:37:34,680
That makes me sound so old.

808
00:37:35,640 --> 00:37:37,520
Come on, let's take a picture of us.

809
00:37:37,600 --> 00:37:38,400
OK!

810
00:37:42,880 --> 00:37:44,760
Why did you make such a mess?

811
00:37:44,880 --> 00:37:46,320
You're onto me?

812
00:37:46,720 --> 00:37:48,680
I used your computer to search something

813
00:37:48,760 --> 00:37:52,680
and I saw a file on the stone coffin case.

814
00:37:53,080 --> 00:37:54,480
What do you want with me?

815
00:37:55,760 --> 00:37:59,240
Yes, I want to know exactly how Ben died.

816
00:37:59,360 --> 00:38:00,320
Was it simply manslaughter?

817
00:38:00,400 --> 00:38:01,600
Or there was more to it?

818
00:38:01,720 --> 00:38:03,040
Why do you want to know?

819
00:38:03,200 --> 00:38:04,560
Who is he to you?

820
00:38:06,960 --> 00:38:08,960
No wonder I found these...

821
00:38:09,080 --> 00:38:10,800
You were having an affair.

822
00:38:13,880 --> 00:38:14,720
Yes!

823
00:38:14,840 --> 00:38:16,240
He was married.

824
00:38:16,320 --> 00:38:19,040
You seem honest, why do you want
to be the other woman?

825
00:38:19,120 --> 00:38:20,640
Why Ben and I were together

826
00:38:20,720 --> 00:38:22,160
is something you'll never understand.

827
00:38:22,280 --> 00:38:25,040
I was wrong. I failed his wife.

828
00:38:25,160 --> 00:38:27,760
But I'm trying my best to look after her.

829
00:38:28,040 --> 00:38:30,000
I want to know the truth
not just for myself.

830
00:38:30,160 --> 00:38:31,720
I'm also doing this for Mary.

831
00:38:31,800 --> 00:38:34,880
I thought I met a big sister
who genuinely cares about me.

832
00:38:35,000 --> 00:38:37,600
But you were using me the whole time.

833
00:38:37,680 --> 00:38:39,680
You're worse than the rest of them.

834
00:38:43,200 --> 00:38:46,720
I suspected you at first,

835
00:38:46,800 --> 00:38:49,760
but I eventually found out
your world is very simple.

836
00:38:49,920 --> 00:38:52,080
People were using you. You were innocent.

837
00:38:52,440 --> 00:38:54,000
I guess the time we spent with each other,

838
00:38:54,080 --> 00:38:55,040
you should be able to sense

839
00:38:55,120 --> 00:38:57,240
everything I told you was the truth.

840
00:38:57,360 --> 00:38:59,640
I truly considered you as a friend.

841
00:39:00,160 --> 00:39:01,920
I'm telling you for the last time.

842
00:39:02,000 --> 00:39:04,880
I told the court everything I knew.

843
00:39:05,080 --> 00:39:07,120
Whatever you want to know, just ask me.

844
00:39:07,200 --> 00:39:09,440
Don't sound me out.

845
00:39:09,600 --> 00:39:12,160
Don't worry, I won't.

846
00:39:12,240 --> 00:39:14,120
Don't lie to me anymore.

847
00:39:14,200 --> 00:39:16,120
I trust you are a good person.

848
00:39:16,240 --> 00:39:18,720
I don't want to lose faith in you.

849
00:39:18,840 --> 00:39:20,640
I have nothing to hide from you.

850
00:39:24,920 --> 00:39:26,200
(The next day)

851
00:39:26,600 --> 00:39:29,600
Everyone wants to make quick money.

852
00:39:29,800 --> 00:39:33,200
Phone scams have high return and low risks.

853
00:39:38,920 --> 00:39:41,440
Brother Kin, I brought your
favorite egg tarts.

854
00:39:41,560 --> 00:39:43,200
Go get me a pack of smokes.

855
00:39:43,680 --> 00:39:44,240
OK.

856
00:39:52,160 --> 00:39:54,560
Don't eat them all. They're too sweet.

857
00:39:54,680 --> 00:39:55,920
You have diabetes.

858
00:39:56,120 --> 00:39:58,960
So? I have medication.

859
00:40:00,080 --> 00:40:02,760
How's the girl?

860
00:40:02,840 --> 00:40:04,880
I had her wrapped around my fingers.

861
00:40:05,000 --> 00:40:07,440
Luckily, you taught me what to do.

862
00:40:07,840 --> 00:40:11,040
Luckily I didn't let those two clowns
toss Ben's phone

863
00:40:11,200 --> 00:40:12,800
and sent you to get it unlocked.

864
00:40:13,440 --> 00:40:15,240
What about his phone?

865
00:40:15,840 --> 00:40:16,800
I'll take it outside and ditch it.

866
00:40:16,960 --> 00:40:19,440
No. Don't let anyone find it.

867
00:40:19,720 --> 00:40:20,800
I'll take care of it.

868
00:40:23,720 --> 00:40:25,360
Can you unlock this?

869
00:40:25,560 --> 00:40:27,840
Did you unlock the phone I brought in?

870
00:40:27,920 --> 00:40:28,880
All set.

871
00:40:31,240 --> 00:40:31,920
Thanks.

872
00:40:38,000 --> 00:40:38,880
What is it?

873
00:40:44,520 --> 00:40:47,640
Brother Kin, Ben's chick approached me.

874
00:40:47,720 --> 00:40:49,680
She's always sounding me out.

875
00:40:49,800 --> 00:40:52,120
I kept shooting off my mouth.

876
00:40:52,200 --> 00:40:53,520
I can't remember if I said the wrong thing.

877
00:40:53,640 --> 00:40:56,320
So? We know more about her.

878
00:40:56,440 --> 00:40:57,840
She should be worried.

879
00:40:58,560 --> 00:41:00,640
What about the thing I asked you to do?

880
00:41:00,720 --> 00:41:01,840
I followed your instructions

881
00:41:01,920 --> 00:41:03,600
and tried to find out where the money was.

882
00:41:04,040 --> 00:41:06,000
Did you leave me the keycard?

883
00:41:06,560 --> 00:41:07,760
Yes, it's for you.

884
00:41:07,880 --> 00:41:10,880
Is this about the legal loopholes?

885
00:41:11,240 --> 00:41:13,840
Don't ask. Just keep it for me.

886
00:41:13,960 --> 00:41:15,440
I read all the messages.

887
00:41:15,560 --> 00:41:18,720
I only know he gave the money
to his girlfriend.

888
00:41:19,440 --> 00:41:21,360
I didn't know it was Cathy.

889
00:41:21,520 --> 00:41:23,280
Ben was quite smart.

890
00:41:23,440 --> 00:41:26,080
No wonder the cops couldn't trace the money.

891
00:41:26,320 --> 00:41:28,960
Since he's dead, we should split the money.

892
00:41:29,160 --> 00:41:30,640
How?

893
00:41:30,760 --> 00:41:32,760
Pretend you didn't know who she was.

894
00:41:32,840 --> 00:41:33,840
Stick with her

895
00:41:33,920 --> 00:41:36,640
and try to find out
where she kept the money.

896
00:41:36,720 --> 00:41:38,240
But to tell a lie like that,

897
00:41:38,320 --> 00:41:40,320
what if she saw through me?

898
00:41:41,200 --> 00:41:43,840
You're so adorable and good at
sweet talking people.

899
00:41:43,960 --> 00:41:45,840
No one would suspect you of
harboring any ulterior motives.

900
00:41:48,280 --> 00:41:50,200
But what's taking so long?

901
00:41:50,840 --> 00:41:52,640
You've been looking since I was in jail.

902
00:41:52,720 --> 00:41:53,920
Now I'm out and you still haven't found it.

903
00:41:54,000 --> 00:41:55,920
I searched through the whole flat.

904
00:41:56,080 --> 00:41:58,560
No money, no keycard.

905
00:41:58,680 --> 00:42:00,400
She almost caught me.

906
00:42:00,520 --> 00:42:01,440
Luckily, I made up a story.

907
00:42:01,560 --> 00:42:03,120
Then it's safe to keep looking.

908
00:42:03,200 --> 00:42:04,200
I'm afraid if I keep it up,

909
00:42:04,280 --> 00:42:07,640
Cathy will ignore me.

910
00:42:07,840 --> 00:42:10,320
Not if you found the money.

911
00:42:13,160 --> 00:42:16,160
I'll take care of you if she won't.

912
00:42:16,240 --> 00:42:20,800
I'll look after you, silly.

913
00:42:21,000 --> 00:42:23,200
Don't tell me you're taking this seriously.

914
00:42:23,320 --> 00:42:25,360
You think she's your friend?

915
00:42:26,280 --> 00:42:28,480
Don't forgot how Ben died.

916
00:42:29,040 --> 00:42:31,200
Don't you feel guilty when you see her?
